# Build artifacts.
/.lake/
*.olean
*.ilean
*.trace
/build/

# Throwaway probes and one-off examples.
/scratch/

# Planning and session handoffs live in the issue tracker or external notes.
HANDOFF.md
ROADMAP.md
/ARCHITECTURE.md

# Environment-emission artifacts are attached to releases or CI runs, not
# committed as potentially stale trust records.
#
# `/attest/*` and not `/attest/`, because git CANNOT re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded -- and exactly one file in here must be
# committed. `review.yaml` is the only contract artifact no machine produces or
# regenerates: CI rebuilds every other attest/ file from scratch on each run,
# so a human review left ignored would vanish on the next clone and C-10 would
# report not_run forever. It is human-authored evidence, not a stale
# measurement, and the reasoning above does not apply to it.
/attest/*
!/attest/review.yaml

# CI scratch, ignored so `worktree_dirty` in environment.json means what it
# says. `mfc env` reads `git status --porcelain`, and `mfc seal` REFUSES a dirty
# tree -- the subject attests a gitCommit, and uncommitted changes make every
# digest in the bundle a true statement about a tree nobody can fetch. Before
# this block the workflow's own venv and audit logs made every CI run "dirty",
# which is a measurement of the workflow rather than of the repository.
/.mfc-venv/
/algebraic-geometry-audit.txt
/bridgeland-audit.txt
/coh-audit.txt
/dg-audit.txt
/enum-decls.txt
/lean-source-check.txt
/stability-condition-audit.txt

# Python bytecode from the gate scripts (scripts/_output.py is imported, so it compiles).
__pycache__/
*.pyc
